              {
                "id": "R3-001",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go:379-383",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "Rotation is guarded by a lock, but the size is checked and the log is then opened in separate steps. A trigger that opened the log before another rotated it keeps appending to the descriptor now named .1, so a few lines can land in the rotated file. Nothing is lost and the effect is small.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go:379-383"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed the full candidate. Rotation, the 0600 narrowing, the bounded stderr copy, field quoting and the refusal of a relative state directory are each pinned by externally observable tests in engine/synctrigger/hardening_test.go and by the golden files.",
              "The no-HOME golden in engine/cmd/testdata/synctrigger-golden/no-home-and-no-state-directory-writes-nothing.golden shows that the program still exits 0, writes error:log on stderr and creates nothing, which keeps the always-exit-0 contract.",
              "boundedBuffer reports full writes, so the MultiWriter does not short-write and the log still receives all output. Both sides of the 64 KiB boundary are tested.",
              "The only golden changes are the log mode (0644 to 0600) and one new case, and the task requested both. I found no BLOCKER or CRITICAL behavior caused by this change."
            ]
          }
